  "dct_description_sm": [
    "<p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:1.5rem; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><span style='font-family:Arial, &quot;sans-serif&quot;;'><a href='https://gis.conservationhalton.net/doc/opendatahub/Metadata/CH_Metadata_WatershedReportCard2018_Groundwater.pdf' style='color:rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Click Here</a> for Metadata. Groundwater quality varies across the watershed based on geology and land use. Nitrite + Nitrate and chloride were used to characterize the quality of groundwater with the watershed indicating excellent conditions.</span><span style='font-family:inherit;'> </span><span style='font-family:Arial, &quot;sans-serif&quot;; background-image:initial; background-position:initial; background-size:initial; background-repeat:initial; background-attachment:initial; background-origin:initial; background-clip:initial;'>Conservation Halton monitored 10 Groundwater wells across the watershed for chloride and nitrate. </span><span style='font-family:Arial, &quot;sans-serif&quot;;'></span></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:1.5rem; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><span style='font-family:Arial, &quot;sans-serif&quot;; background-image:initial; background-position:initial; background-size:initial; background-repeat:initial; background-attachment:initial; background-origin:initial; background-clip:initial;'>The grading scale is as follows, A - Excellent; B - Good; C - Fair; D - Poor; and F - Very Poor.</span></p>"
